<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.13.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01488</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.13.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>947d5e35-a252-4d4b-8138-3682ad62e2b0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
        <exercise id="_2db26d10-04e4-4540-a272-30228d06b376" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00001">Here is a graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, an insect population, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>w</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> weeks after it was first measured. The population
          grows exponentially. 
          <media alt=""><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_10_01.jpg" width="300"/></media></para><para id="para-00002">
              What is the weekly factor of growth for the insect population?</para>
        
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            
            <para id="para-00003">Try again. Revisit activity 5.13.2. 
    </para>
            <para id="para-00004">The correct answer is 3.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e8f10c0a-032d-4ab5-8933-ce06c9f51e2d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00005">What was the population when it was first measured?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            
            <para id="para-00006">Try again. Revisit activity 5.13.2. 
    </para>
            <para id="para-00007">The correct answer is 300.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="cbfdb135-dc79-4528-bb35-0db6647ca15f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00008">Write an equation relating <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>w</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00009">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00010"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>300</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>w</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00011"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>300</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>w</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00012"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>300</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>w</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00013"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>300</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>w</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            
            <para id="para-00014">Try again. Revisit activity 5.13.2. 
    </para>
            <para id="para-00015">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>300</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>w</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_81c70864-a6bf-4d9e-83de-c1d4540d165c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00016">Here is a graph of the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
              
              <media alt=""><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_10_02.jpg" width="300"/></media><emphasis>
            Select three</emphasis> possible values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            
            <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activities 5.13.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_20429ef0-bf0e-4a6b-8570-8d3531211391" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00019">The function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is given by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, and the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is given by
          <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
          Here are graphs of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.
          
          <media alt="Graph of two decreasing exponential functions, xy-plane, origin O."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_10_03.svg"/></media></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            
            <para id="para-00020">Try again. Revisit activities 5.13.3 – 5.13.4. Are you using it
        the right way?
    </para>
            <para id="para-00021">The correct answer is Graph 1. The growth factor for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is greater than that of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, so <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>
        lies above <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> on the graph.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="bd2f7076-6229-4987-ad09-6ec00a25b88d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00022">The function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>. The function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.
          Here are graphs of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.
          
          <media alt="Graph of two increasing exponential functions, labeled f and g, xy-plane, origin O."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_10_04.svg"/></media></para>
          <para id="para-00023">
              In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is greater than/less than 50.</para>
        
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            
            <para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activities 5.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00025">The correct answer is greater than. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is above the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="cd5259b9-f0b7-48fb-a1a4-bc137b5b7781" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00026">In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is greater than/less than 3.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            
            <para id="para-00027">Try again. Revisit activities 5.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00028">The correct answer is less than. In <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is less than 3 (but still larger than 1) because the growth
        rate of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is faster than the growth rate of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>